{"page":78,"verses":[{"verse_key":"4:7","surah":4,"ayah":7,"ar_uthmani":"لِّلرِّجَالِ نَصِيبٌ مِّمَّا تَرَكَ ٱلْوَٰلِدَانِ وَٱلْأَقْرَبُونَ وَلِلنِّسَآءِ نَصِيبٌ مِّمَّا تَرَكَ ٱلْوَٰلِدَانِ وَٱلْأَقْرَبُونَ مِمَّا قَلَّ مِنْهُ أَوْ كَثُرَ ۚ نَصِيبًا مَّفْرُوضًا","en_translation_id":85,"en":"Men shall have a share in what their parents and closest relatives leave, and women shall have a share in what their parents and closest relatives leave, whether the legacy be small or large: this is ordained by God.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"لِّلرِّجَالِ","en_gloss":"For the men","transliteration":"lilrrijāli","verse_key":"4:7"},{"pos":2,"ar":"نَصِيبٌۭ","en_gloss":"a portion","transliteration":"naṣībun","verse_key":"4:7"},{"pos":3,"ar":"مِّمَّا","en_gloss":"of what","transliteration":"mimmā","verse_key":"4:7"},{"pos":4,"ar":"تَرَكَ","en_gloss":"(is) left","transliteration":"taraka","verse_key":"4:7"},{"pos":5,"ar":"ٱلْوَٰلِدَانِ","en_gloss":"(by) the parents","transliteration":"l-wālidāni","verse_key":"4:7"},{"pos":6,"ar":"وَٱلْأَقْرَبُونَ","en_gloss":"and the near relatives","transliteration":"wal-aqrabūna","verse_key":"4:7"},{"pos":7,"ar":"وَلِلنِّسَآءِ","en_gloss":"and for the women","transliteration":"walilnnisāi","verse_key":"4:7"},{"pos":8,"ar":"نَصِيبٌۭ","en_gloss":"a portion","transliteration":"naṣībun","verse_key":"4:7"},{"pos":9,"ar":"مِّمَّا","en_gloss":"of what","transliteration":"mimmā","verse_key":"4:7"},{"pos":10,"ar":"تَرَكَ","en_gloss":"(is) left","transliteration":"taraka","verse_key":"4:7"},{"pos":11,"ar":"ٱلْوَٰلِدَانِ","en_gloss":"(by) parents","transliteration":"l-wālidāni","verse_key":"4:7"},{"pos":12,"ar":"وَٱلْأَقْرَبُونَ","en_gloss":"and the near relatives","transliteration":"wal-aqrabūna","verse_key":"4:7"},{"pos":13,"ar":"مِمَّا","en_gloss":"of what","transliteration":"mimmā","verse_key":"4:7"},{"pos":14,"ar":"قَلَّ","en_gloss":"(is) little","transliteration":"qalla","verse_key":"4:7"},{"pos":15,"ar":"مِنْهُ","en_gloss":"of it","transliteration":"min'hu","verse_key":"4:7"},{"pos":16,"ar":"أَوْ","en_gloss":"or","transliteration":"aw","verse_key":"4:7"},{"pos":17,"ar":"كَثُرَ ۚ","en_gloss":"much ","transliteration":"kathura","verse_key":"4:7"},{"pos":18,"ar":"نَصِيبًۭا","en_gloss":"a portion","transliteration":"naṣīban","verse_key":"4:7"},{"pos":19,"ar":"مَّفْرُوضًۭا","en_gloss":"obligatory","transliteration":"mafrūḍan","verse_key":"4:7"},{"pos":20,"ar":"٧","en_gloss":"(7)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"4:7"}]},{"verse_key":"4:8","surah":4,"ayah":8,"ar_uthmani":"وَإِذَا حَضَرَ ٱلْقِسْمَةَ أُو۟لُوا۟ ٱلْقُرْبَىٰ وَٱلْيَتَـٰمَىٰ وَٱلْمَسَـٰكِينُ فَٱرْزُقُوهُم مِّنْهُ وَقُولُوا۟ لَهُمْ قَوْلًا مَّعْرُوفًا","en_translation_id":85,"en":"If other relatives, orphans, or needy people are present at the distribution, give them something too, and speak kindly to them.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"وَإِذَا","en_gloss":"And when","transliteration":"wa-idhā","verse_key":"4:8"},{"pos":2,"ar":"حَضَرَ","en_gloss":"present","transliteration":"ḥaḍara","verse_key":"4:8"},{"pos":3,"ar":"ٱلْقِسْمَةَ","en_gloss":"(at) the (time of) division","transliteration":"l-qis'mata","verse_key":"4:8"},{"pos":4,"ar":"أُو۟لُوا۟","en_gloss":"(of)","transliteration":"ulū","verse_key":"4:8"},{"pos":5,"ar":"ٱلْقُرْبَىٰ","en_gloss":"the relatives","transliteration":"l-qur'bā","verse_key":"4:8"},{"pos":6,"ar":"وَٱلْيَتَـٰمَىٰ","en_gloss":"and the orphans","transliteration":"wal-yatāmā","verse_key":"4:8"},{"pos":7,"ar":"وَٱلْمَسَـٰكِينُ","en_gloss":"and the poor","transliteration":"wal-masākīnu","verse_key":"4:8"},{"pos":8,"ar":"فَٱرْزُقُوهُم","en_gloss":"then provide them","transliteration":"fa-ur'zuqūhum","verse_key":"4:8"},{"pos":9,"ar":"مِّنْهُ","en_gloss":"from it","transliteration":"min'hu","verse_key":"4:8"},{"pos":10,"ar":"وَقُولُوا۟","en_gloss":"and speak","transliteration":"waqūlū","verse_key":"4:8"},{"pos":11,"ar":"لَهُمْ","en_gloss":"to them","transliteration":"lahum","verse_key":"4:8"},{"pos":12,"ar":"قَوْلًۭا","en_gloss":"words","transliteration":"qawlan","verse_key":"4:8"},{"pos":13,"ar":"مَّعْرُوفًۭا","en_gloss":"(of) kindness","transliteration":"maʿrūfan","verse_key":"4:8"},{"pos":14,"ar":"٨","en_gloss":"(8)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"4:8"}]},{"verse_key":"4:9","surah":4,"ayah":9,"ar_uthmani":"وَلْيَخْشَ ٱلَّذِينَ لَوْ تَرَكُوا۟ مِنْ خَلْفِهِمْ ذُرِّيَّةً ضِعَـٰفًا خَافُوا۟ عَلَيْهِمْ فَلْيَتَّقُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ وَلْيَقُولُوا۟ قَوْلًا سَدِيدًا","en_translation_id":85,"en":"Let those who would fear for the future of their own helpless children, if they were to die, show the same concern [for orphans]; let them be mindful of God and speak out for justice.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"وَلْيَخْشَ","en_gloss":"And let fear ","transliteration":"walyakhsha","verse_key":"4:9"},{"pos":2,"ar":"ٱلَّذِينَ","en_gloss":"those who","transliteration":"alladhīna","verse_key":"4:9"},{"pos":3,"ar":"لَوْ","en_gloss":"if","transliteration":"law","verse_key":"4:9"},{"pos":4,"ar":"تَرَكُوا۟","en_gloss":"they left","transliteration":"tarakū","verse_key":"4:9"},{"pos":5,"ar":"مِنْ","en_gloss":"from","transliteration":"min","verse_key":"4:9"},{"pos":6,"ar":"خَلْفِهِمْ","en_gloss":"behind","transliteration":"khalfihim","verse_key":"4:9"},{"pos":7,"ar":"ذُرِّيَّةًۭ","en_gloss":"offspring","transliteration":"dhurriyyatan","verse_key":"4:9"},{"pos":8,"ar":"ضِعَـٰفًا","en_gloss":"weak","transliteration":"ḍiʿāfan","verse_key":"4:9"},{"pos":9,"ar":"خَافُوا۟","en_gloss":"(and) they would have feared","transliteration":"khāfū","verse_key":"4:9"},{"pos":10,"ar":"عَلَيْهِمْ","en_gloss":"about them","transliteration":"ʿalayhim","verse_key":"4:9"},{"pos":11,"ar":"فَلْيَتَّقُوا۟","en_gloss":"So let them fear","transliteration":"falyattaqū","verse_key":"4:9"},{"pos":12,"ar":"ٱللَّهَ","en_gloss":"Allah","transliteration":"l-laha","verse_key":"4:9"},{"pos":13,"ar":"وَلْيَقُولُوا۟","en_gloss":"and let them speak","transliteration":"walyaqūlū","verse_key":"4:9"},{"pos":14,"ar":"قَوْلًۭا","en_gloss":"words","transliteration":"qawlan","verse_key":"4:9"},{"pos":15,"ar":"سَدِيدًا","en_gloss":"appropriate","transliteration":"sadīdan","verse_key":"4:9"},{"pos":16,"ar":"٩","en_gloss":"(9)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"4:9"}]},{"verse_key":"4:10","surah":4,"ayah":10,"ar_uthmani":"إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ يَأْكُلُونَ أَمْوَٰلَ ٱلْيَتَـٰمَىٰ ظُلْمًا إِنَّمَا يَأْكُلُونَ فِى بُطُونِهِمْ نَارًا ۖ وَسَيَصْلَوْنَ سَعِيرًا","en_translation_id":85,"en":"Those who consume the property of orphans unjustly are actually swallowing fire into their own bellies: they will burn in the blazing Flame.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"إِنَّ","en_gloss":"Indeed","transliteration":"inna","verse_key":"4:10"},{"pos":2,"ar":"ٱلَّذِينَ","en_gloss":"those who","transliteration":"alladhīna","verse_key":"4:10"},{"pos":3,"ar":"يَأْكُلُونَ","en_gloss":"consume","transliteration":"yakulūna","verse_key":"4:10"},{"pos":4,"ar":"أَمْوَٰلَ","en_gloss":"wealth","transliteration":"amwāla","verse_key":"4:10"},{"pos":5,"ar":"ٱلْيَتَـٰمَىٰ","en_gloss":"(of) the orphans","transliteration":"l-yatāmā","verse_key":"4:10"},{"pos":6,"ar":"ظُلْمًا","en_gloss":"wrongfully","transliteration":"ẓul'man","verse_key":"4:10"},{"pos":7,"ar":"إِنَّمَا","en_gloss":"only","transliteration":"innamā","verse_key":"4:10"},{"pos":8,"ar":"يَأْكُلُونَ","en_gloss":"they consume","transliteration":"yakulūna","verse_key":"4:10"},{"pos":9,"ar":"فِى","en_gloss":"in","transliteration":"fī","verse_key":"4:10"},{"pos":10,"ar":"بُطُونِهِمْ","en_gloss":"their bellies","transliteration":"buṭūnihim","verse_key":"4:10"},{"pos":11,"ar":"نَارًۭا ۖ","en_gloss":"fire","transliteration":"nāran","verse_key":"4:10"},{"pos":12,"ar":"وَسَيَصْلَوْنَ","en_gloss":"and they will be burned","transliteration":"wasayaṣlawna","verse_key":"4:10"},{"pos":13,"ar":"سَعِيرًۭا","en_gloss":"(in) a Blazing Fire","transliteration":"saʿīran","verse_key":"4:10"},{"pos":14,"ar":"١٠","en_gloss":"(10)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"4:10"}]},{"verse_key":"4:11","surah":4,"ayah":11,"ar_uthmani":"يُوصِيكُمُ ٱللَّهُ فِىٓ أَوْلَـٰدِكُمْ ۖ لِلذَّكَرِ مِثْلُ حَظِّ ٱلْأُنثَيَيْنِ ۚ فَإِن كُنَّ نِسَآءً فَوْقَ ٱثْنَتَيْنِ فَلَهُنَّ ثُلُثَا مَا تَرَكَ ۖ وَإِن كَانَتْ وَٰحِدَةً فَلَهَا ٱلنِّصْفُ ۚ وَلِأَبَوَيْهِ لِكُلِّ وَٰحِدٍ مِّنْهُمَا ٱلسُّدُسُ مِمَّا تَرَكَ إِن كَانَ لَهُۥ وَلَدٌ ۚ فَإِن لَّمْ يَكُن لَّهُۥ وَلَدٌ وَوَرِثَهُۥٓ أَبَوَاهُ فَلِأُمِّهِ ٱلثُّلُثُ ۚ فَإِن كَانَ لَهُۥٓ إِخْوَةٌ فَلِأُمِّهِ ٱلسُّدُسُ ۚ مِنۢ بَعْدِ وَصِيَّةٍ يُوصِى بِهَآ أَوْ دَيْنٍ ۗ ءَابَآؤُكُمْ وَأَبْنَآؤُكُمْ لَا تَدْرُونَ أَيُّهُمْ أَقْرَبُ لَكُمْ نَفْعًا ۚ فَرِيضَةً مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ ۗ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ كَانَ عَلِيمًا حَكِيمًا","en_translation_id":85,"en":"Concerning your children, God commands you that a son should have the equivalent share of two daughters. If there are only daughters, two or more should share two-thirds of the inheritance, if one, she should have half. Parents inherit a sixth each if the deceased leaves children; if he leaves no children and his parents are his sole heirs, his mother has a third, unless he has brothers, in which case she has a sixth. [In all cases, the distribution comes] after payment of any bequests or debts. You cannot know which of your parents or your children is more beneficial to you: this is a law from God, and He is all knowing, all wise.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"يُوصِيكُمُ","en_gloss":"Instructs you","transliteration":"yūṣīkumu","verse_key":"4:11"},{"pos":2,"ar":"ٱللَّهُ","en_gloss":"Allah","transliteration":"l-lahu","verse_key":"4:11"},{"pos":3,"ar":"فِىٓ","en_gloss":"concerning","transliteration":"fī","verse_key":"4:11"},{"pos":4,"ar":"أَوْلَـٰدِكُمْ ۖ","en_gloss":"your children ","transliteration":"awlādikum","verse_key":"4:11"},{"pos":5,"ar":"لِلذَّكَرِ","en_gloss":"for the male","transliteration":"lildhakari","verse_key":"4:11"},{"pos":6,"ar":"مِثْلُ","en_gloss":"like","transliteration":"mith'lu","verse_key":"4:11"},{"pos":7,"ar":"حَظِّ","en_gloss":"(the) portion","transliteration":"ḥaẓẓi","verse_key":"4:11"},{"pos":8,"ar":"ٱلْأُنثَيَيْنِ ۚ","en_gloss":"(of) two females","transliteration":"l-unthayayni","verse_key":"4:11"},{"pos":9,"ar":"فَإِن","en_gloss":"But if","transliteration":"fa-in","verse_key":"4:11"},{"pos":10,"ar":"كُنَّ","en_gloss":"there are","transliteration":"kunna","verse_key":"4:11"},{"pos":11,"ar":"نِسَآءًۭ","en_gloss":"(only) women","transliteration":"nisāan","verse_key":"4:11"},{"pos":12,"ar":"فَوْقَ","en_gloss":"more (than)","transliteration":"fawqa","verse_key":"4:11"},{"pos":13,"ar":"ٱثْنَتَيْنِ","en_gloss":"two","transliteration":"ith'natayni","verse_key":"4:11"},{"pos":14,"ar":"فَلَهُنَّ","en_gloss":"then for them","transliteration":"falahunna","verse_key":"4:11"},{"pos":15,"ar":"ثُلُثَا","en_gloss":"two thirds","transliteration":"thuluthā","verse_key":"4:11"},{"pos":16,"ar":"مَا","en_gloss":"(of) what","transliteration":"mā","verse_key":"4:11"},{"pos":17,"ar":"تَرَكَ ۖ","en_gloss":"he left","transliteration":"taraka","verse_key":"4:11"},{"pos":18,"ar":"وَإِن","en_gloss":"And if","transliteration":"wa-in","verse_key":"4:11"},{"pos":19,"ar":"كَانَتْ","en_gloss":"(there) is","transliteration":"kānat","verse_key":"4:11"},{"pos":20,"ar":"وَٰحِدَةًۭ","en_gloss":"(only) one","transliteration":"wāḥidatan","verse_key":"4:11"},{"pos":21,"ar":"فَلَهَا","en_gloss":"then for her","transliteration":"falahā","verse_key":"4:11"},{"pos":22,"ar":"ٱلنِّصْفُ ۚ","en_gloss":"(is) half","transliteration":"l-niṣ'fu","verse_key":"4:11"},{"pos":23,"ar":"وَلِأَبَوَيْهِ","en_gloss":"And for his parents","transliteration":"wali-abawayhi","verse_key":"4:11"},{"pos":24,"ar":"لِكُلِّ","en_gloss":"for each","transliteration":"likulli","verse_key":"4:11"},{"pos":25,"ar":"وَٰحِدٍۢ","en_gloss":"one","transliteration":"wāḥidin","verse_key":"4:11"},{"pos":26,"ar":"مِّنْهُمَا","en_gloss":"of them","transliteration":"min'humā","verse_key":"4:11"},{"pos":27,"ar":"ٱلسُّدُسُ","en_gloss":"a sixth","transliteration":"l-sudusu","verse_key":"4:11"},{"pos":28,"ar":"مِمَّا","en_gloss":"of what","transliteration":"mimmā","verse_key":"4:11"},{"pos":29,"ar